  "could_not_say": {
    "types": [
      "01 25"
    ],
    "why": "These types changed nothing this note could hear, so they carry no evidence either way about a modulator. An effect that never reached the signal path repeats exactly as well as one standing still, and reading the second from the first would be a verdict on the routing, or on the note, wearing the effect's name.",
    "inside_the_calibration_gap": {
      "types": [
        "01 25"
      ],
      "why": "These types opened a gap between the two settings' repeatability, but the setting that repeated worse landed between the worst a level change alone has produced on this chain and the bar a modulator is claimed above. Inside that band the calibration does not separate the two explanations: a shallow modulator and a level change at a poor signal to noise both reach it. They are reported here rather than in either pile, because the bar has to fall somewhere and a reading just under it is not the same fact as a reading far under it."
    }
  },
